# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: install-release-staging-divergence — `make install` and the release tarball produce different program layouts
#+STATUS: OPEN
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -

* Symptom (pjb, 2026-08-23)

Building master, then =make install= on MS-Windows, put =alfe-sbcl.exe= and
=alfe.exe= in =/opt/local/bin=, whereas the release tarball places the per-Lisp
images under a =libexec= subtree. The two SHOULD be the same tree — a release is
just a packaged install — so this divergence is a bug.

* Root cause — programs are staged two different ways

The LIBRARIES phase is already unified, and is the model to copy:

- =install-libraries= = =stage-libraries= + =copy-stage $(STAGE_LIBRARIES)=
- =release-libraries= = =stage-libraries= + =pack $(STAGE_LIBRARIES)=

Both consume the SAME =stage-libraries= tree. Good.

The PROGRAMS phase is NOT unified:

- =install-programs= (top Makefile) = =stage-programs= + =copy-stage
  $(STAGE_PROGRAMS)=. =stage-programs= runs each subproject's own
  =install-programs= into =$(STAGE_PROGRAMS)=, which installs the per-Lisp
  images DIRECTLY INTO =bin/= (clautolisp/Makefile, autolisp-front-end/Makefile:
  =BIN_INSTALL_DIR=), plus the bare launcher, the test harness, the alref
  reference libs, autolisp-benchmark, and =run-file-compat= /
  =run-alfe-conformance= under =libexec/<subproject>/=.
- =release-programs= (top Makefile) is a SEPARATE hand-rolled recipe that does
  NOT call =stage-programs=. It writes a *dispatch-wrapper* layout: the three
  main images (=clautolisp-<l>=, =read-autolisp-<l>=, =alfe-<l>=) go under
  =libexec/clautolisp/binaries/<os>/<arch>/=, and =bin/{clautolisp,alfe,
  read-autolisp}= are copies of =tools/packaging/dispatch.sh= (+ =.cmd= on
  Windows) that pick the right image at run time.

So the two diverge on TWO axes, not one:

1. *Layout*: images in =bin/= (install) vs =libexec/clautolisp/binaries/<os>/<arch>/=
   + a dispatch launcher (release).
2. *Content*: full set — harness, alref libs, benchmark, run-file-compat
   (install) vs the three main binaries only (release).

* Constraint that forces the dispatch layout

The =-all= artefact is the UNPACKED UNION of every per-target binaries tarball
(collect phase). It merges each target's =libexec/.../ <os>/<arch>/= subtree so
all platforms' binaries coexist under one tree with a single dispatch launcher.
The plain =bin/= install layout cannot union across platforms: extensionless
Linux and macOS images collide (=bin/clautolisp-sbcl= from two OSes/arches), and
the bare launcher differs (POSIX symlink vs Windows =.exe=). So the dispatch /
=libexec/<os>/<arch>/= layout is REQUIRED for the multi-platform release and
cannot simply be replaced by the =bin/= layout.

* Proposed fix — one staging, mirroring the libraries phase

Make the dispatch layout canonical and single-sourced, exactly as
=stage-libraries= already is:

1. Move =release-programs='s hand-rolled staging body INTO =stage-programs=, so
   =stage-programs= writes the dispatch layout (=libexec/clautolisp/binaries/
   <os>/<arch>/= + =bin/= dispatch wrappers) into =$(STAGE_PROGRAMS)=.
2. =release-programs= becomes =stage-programs= + =pack $(STAGE_PROGRAMS)= (one
   line, like release-libraries). No more bespoke layout.
3. =install-programs= is already =stage-programs= + =copy-stage=, so it then
   installs the SAME dispatch tree — matching the tarball. =make install= gives
   =bin/{clautolisp,alfe,read-autolisp}= dispatch launchers + images under
   =libexec/...=.
4. collect / =-all= keep working unchanged: they already expect the
   =libexec/<os>/<arch>/= subtree the new =stage-programs= produces.

Two DECISIONS to settle before implementing (why this is filed, not just
patched blind — it changes =make install= for every user and touches the
release, which has a history of breakage):

- *Content reconciliation*: =stage-programs= currently also stages the test
  harness, alref reference libs, autolisp-benchmark and the =run-*= libexec
  helpers, which the release's programs artefact does NOT ship. Decide whether
  the unified staging keeps them (install-only extras, guarded so the release
  pack excludes them) or drops them. A naïve swap either bloats the release with
  test harnesses or strips them from =make install=.
- *dispatch launcher on a single-platform install*: confirm =dispatch.sh= /
  =dispatch.cmd= resolve the sole =<os>/<arch>= subtree correctly for a plain
  one-platform =make install= (they were written for the multi-platform union).

* Acceptance criteria

- =make install= and the per-target release binaries artefact unpack to the
  identical program tree for a given os/arch (same paths, same launchers).
- The =-all= multi-platform union still works (each platform's
  =libexec/<os>/<arch>/= coexists under one dispatch launcher).
- A test asserts the two trees match (e.g. stage-programs then diff its layout
  against the release pack's), so they cannot silently drift again.
- No regression in what =make install= delivers (or a deliberate, documented
  content change).

* Notes

- Subproject-level =make -C <subproject> install= may keep its own =bin/=
  layout as a dev convenience; the divergence that matters is the TOP-LEVEL
  install vs the release, which this unifies.
- Model to copy verbatim: =install-libraries= / =release-libraries= /
  =stage-libraries= in the top Makefile.
